    <string name="settings_howto_step1_title">1. Select Your File</string>
    <string name="settings_howto_step1_body">Tap the module from the bottom nav or hub cards, then tap Select File and choose your Excel report from device storage.</string>
    <string name="settings_howto_step2_title">2. Process the Report</string>
    <string name="settings_howto_step2_body">Tap Process. The app analyses the file using built-in Python logic and displays a summary.</string>
    <string name="settings_howto_step3_title">3. Export or Share</string>
    <string name="settings_howto_step3_body">Tap Export Report to save to your Downloads folder, or tap Share to send via WhatsApp, Email, or any other app.</string>
    <string name="settings_howto_collections_title">Collections Module</string>
    <string name="settings_howto_collections_body">Requires two files: the Start-of-Day (SOD) file and the current file. Select each with the labelled buttons then press Process.</string>
    <string name="settings_howto_loantracker_title">Loan Week Tracker</string>
    <string name="settings_howto_loantracker_body">Uses the disbursement report with built-in 2024 product logic (KES 3,000-49,000, 5/7/10/12-week terms) to calculate weekly tracking metrics.</string>
    <string name="settings_howto_branch_title">Branch Comparison</string>
    <string name="settings_howto_branch_body">Upload separate Income, CR, and Disbursement files to compare KPIs across all branches in one consolidated report.</string>
    <string name="settings_howto_premium_title">Premium Features</string>
    <string name="settings_howto_premium_body">Some modules require a subscription. The free plan has limited daily reports. Upgrade via the Subscription section above.</string>
